        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nI need to observe every intermediate change of a key-value entity via a consumer. Workable?",
          "label": "evals/akka-sdk-consumers/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "d03521c654409d4475c887a69078a2496ec5cd2ac7f26ff99487272af8c1f470",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No, not with a key-value entity. A `@Consume.FromKeyValueEntity` consumer is only guaranteed the most recent state, so intermediate changes can be skipped, especially when updates come faster than the consumer processes them.\n\nYour options:\n\n- **Switch to an event-sourced entity** (recommended). A `@Consume.FromEventSourcedEntity` consumer sees every event in order, at-least-once. This is the right model when each change matters.\n- **Keep the KV entity and emit changes yourself.** Have the entity's command handler also write each change to somewhere durable, such as a separate event-sourced entity acting as an audit log. Consume that instead. Only do this if you can't migrate the entity.\n\nWhichever you pick, delivery is at-least-once and the SDK doesn't dedup, so make the consumer idempotent."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
